event: message
data: {"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Returning 2 cases (offset 0)\n\n**Case 1: European countries are facing insolvency because of their support of Ukraine**\n\n**ID:** 34847d2e-4b1f-4f52-a290-429ab777a949\n\n**Claim:**\nThe US-Russia war in Ukraine is economically ruining Europe. This is part of the US-initiated WWIII. Some European countries which have been supporting Ukraine financially and militarily, are facing insolvency.\n\n**Fact Check:**\nThis claim is made in the context of Russia’s full-scale invasion of Ukraine to push a recurring pro-Kremlin disinformation narrative: that international aid to Ukraine dramatically harms the economic situation of the countries providing it. It is also consistent with recurring pro-Kremlin disinformation narratives claiming that the West / the US / Europe instigated the war in Ukraine and that Western and European countries pursue an allegedly belligerent and hostile agenda against Russia.This article manipulatively suggests that pro-Ukrainian policies put European countries on the brink of insolvency. While the EU countries are experiencing slowdown in growth in 2026 as energy shock drives up inflation, the economic forecast suggests a modest 1.4% growth in the EU for 2027. While some EU countries are facing fiscal pressure, there is no evidence that support of Ukraine was among significant reasons behind it.Russia is the only country responsible for the invasion of Ukraine. It has been coming up with different explanations and pretexts for its aggression since the beginning of hostilities. Many European countries provide Ukraine with military and technical assistance to help it repel Russia’s aggression and restore its sovereignty within its internationally recognised 1991 borders. Western / European countries are not at war with Russia, nor are they planning to invade Russia. Ukraine receives weapons with the aim of restoring its territorial integrity within its internationally recognised b[OT(1] order. The EU’s financial support for Ukraine is also an investment in Europe’s own security.See earlier disinformation cases alleging that the West wanted to exhaust Russia through the war in Ukraine, that the EU will choose between food and heating this winter, that Poland is to unleash the all-European war, and that the EU and NATO that want to wage war against Russia.\n\n**Date:** 11/16/2026\n\n**Countries:** Europe, Russia, Ukraine, US\n\n**Keywords:** War against Ukraine, Economic difficulties, World War III\n\n**Source URL:** https://euvsdisinfo.eu/report/european-countries-are-facing-inslvency-due-to-their-support-of-ukraine/\n\n**Disinformation Links:**\n- Грыгуч: США хотят немедленно уволить Зеленского, но пока не могут (Russian)\n  URL: https://sputnik.by/20261112/gryguch-ssha-khotyat-nemedlenno-uvolit-zelenskogo-no-poka-ne-mogut-1112655867.html\n  Snapshot: https://archive.euvsd.info/snapshots/000f9247-834e-4f1e-8a5a-000efaaafc2c\n\n---\n\n**Case 2: Aggression against Russia has become a moral obligation for Europe**\n\n**ID:** 8a3ac496-c6fc-4222-b037-29ffd0e8631b\n\n**Claim:**\nAny society or political movement, in order to develop politically, requires an adversary, and this need is deeply ingrained in our collective consciousness.For a long time, the Ottoman Empire successfully fulfilled this role for Europe. However, with the decline of the Ottomans, Turkey began to transform from a “dangerous outsider” to the “sick man of Europe”. This meant that European governments desperately needed another “dangerous outsider”, and they gradually began to assign this role to the Russian Empire.This transformation occurred within a few decades: while they had seen Alexander I as a Christian ruler who defeated the “atheist” Napoleon, Nicholas I had become, in reality, a “strangler of freedom” and the “gendarme of Europe”.Since Russia had now become the “dangerous outsider”, aggression against it has become a moral obligation.\n\n**Fact Check:**\nThis is a recurring pro-Kremlin disinformation narrative that portrays European hostility towards Russia as a historically engineered phenomenon, driven by an alleged need to manufacture an external enemy to unite European societies. It reduces centuries of complex diplomatic relations to a simplistic conspiracy in which European powers supposedly invented the Russian threat to justify aggression.The historical record contradicts this interpretation. Following Napoleon's defeat in 1815, Tsar Alexander I was widely recognised in Europe as one of the architects of the post-Napoleonic European security order. Russia played a central role in the Congress of Vienna and became a founding member of the Holy Alliance alongside Austria and Prussia. It was also a key participant in the Concert of Europe, the diplomatic framework established to preserve peace and manage conflicts among the great powers.The subsequent deterioration of Russia's image under Nicholas I was not the result of Europeans inventing a new enemy. Nicholas acquired the reputation of the &quot;gendarme of Europe&quot; because of his own domestic and foreign policies, including the violent suppression of the Polish uprising of 1830–1831 and Russia's military intervention in Hungary in 1849 to crush the Hungarian revolution. His opposition to liberal and independence movements placed Russia at odds with political forces across Europe.The same historical revisionism is being applied to Russia's full-scale invasion of Ukraine. The Kremlin portrays the war as a defensive response to Western encirclement, NATO expansion and alleged threats from Ukrainian nationalism, thereby shifting responsibility for its aggression onto Ukraine and its Western partners. This framing presents Russia's military intervention as historically justified and opposition to it as hostility towards Russia itself.See similar cases that Europe has always been trying to weaken Russia, that Europe is ready to harm itself just to harm Russia, and that Poland uses Russia as its external enemy presenting it almost worse than the German nazis.\n\n**Date:** 11/16/2026\n\n**Countries:** Europe, Russia, Turkey\n\n**Keywords:** Russian world, Anti-Russian\n\n**Source URL:** https://euvsdisinfo.eu/report/for-europe-aggression-against-russia-has-become-a-moral-obligation/\n\n**Disinformation Links:**\n- الأسباب التي تجعل جميع حروب روسيا مع أوروبا حروبًا وجودية (Arabic)\n  URL: https://rtarabic.com/press/1852172-%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%A3%D8%B3%D8%A8%D8%A7%D8%A8-%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%AA%D9%8A-%D8%AA%D8%AC%D8%B9%D9%84-%D8%AC%D9%85%D9%8A%D8%B9-%D8%AD%D8%B1%D9%88%D8%A8-%D8%B1%D9%88%D8%B3%D9%8A%D8%A7-%D9%85%D8%B9-%D8%A3%D9%88%D8%B1%D9%88%D8%A8%D8%A7-%D8%AD%D8%B1%D9%88%D8%A8%D8%A7-%D9%88%D8%AC%D9%88%D8%AF%D9%8A%D8%A9/\n  Snapshot: https://archive.euvsd.info/snapshots/8a0599d4-74f4-4190-8b61-20f7f2590de8\n\n\n**Database Info:**\n- Total cases: 19873\n- Current page: 1 of 9937\n- Has next page: Yes\n"}],"structuredContent":{"total":19873,"offset":0,"limit":2,"cases":[{"id":"34847d2e-4b1f-4f52-a290-429ab777a949","title":"European countries are facing insolvency because of their support of Ukraine","claim":"<p>The US-Russia war in Ukraine is economically ruining Europe. This is part of the US-initiated WWIII. Some European countries which have been supporting Ukraine financially and militarily, are facing insolvency.</p>","fact":"<p>This claim is made in the context of Russia’s full-scale invasion of Ukraine to push a recurring pro-Kremlin disinformation narrative: that <a href=\"#\" data-seo-href=\"aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuaWZ3LWtpZWwuZGUvdG9waWNzL3dhci1hZ2FpbnN0LXVrcmFpbmUvdWtyYWluZS1zdXBwb3J0LXRyYWNrZXIv\">international aid to Ukraine</a> dramatically harms the economic situation of the countries providing it. It is also consistent with recurring pro-Kremlin disinformation narratives claiming that the West / the US / Europe instigated the war in Ukraine and that Western and European countries pursue an allegedly <a href=\"https://euvsdisinfo.eu/disinformation-about-the-current-russia-ukraine-conflict-seven-myths-debunked/\">belligerent and hostile agenda against Russia</a>.</p><p>This article manipulatively suggests that pro-Ukrainian policies put European countries on the brink of insolvency. While the EU countries are experiencing slowdown in growth in 2026 as energy shock drives up inflation, the economic forecast <a href=\"#\" data-seo-href=\"aHR0cHM6Ly9lY29ub215LWZpbmFuY2UuZWMuZXVyb3BhLmV1L2Vjb25vbWljLWZvcmVjYXN0LWFuZC1zdXJ2ZXlzL2Vjb25vbWljLWZvcmVjYXN0cy9zcHJpbmctMjAyNi1lY29ub21pYy1mb3JlY2FzdC1zbG93ZG93bi1ncm93dGgtZW5lcmd5LXNob2NrLWRyaXZlcy1pbmZsYXRpb25fZW4=\">suggests</a> a modest 1.4% growth in the EU for 2027. While some EU countries are facing fiscal pressure, there is no evidence that support of Ukraine was among significant reasons behind it.</p><p>Russia is the only country responsible for the invasion of Ukraine. It has been coming up with <a href=\"https://euvsdisinfo.eu/disinformation-about-the-current-russia-ukraine-conflict-seven-myths-debunked/\">different explanations and pretexts</a> for its aggression since the beginning of hostilities. Many European countries provide Ukraine with military and technical assistance to help it repel Russia’s aggression and restore its sovereignty within its internationally recognised 1991 borders. Western / European countries are not at war with Russia, nor are they planning to invade Russia. Ukraine receives weapons with the aim of restoring its territorial integrity within its internationally recognised b[OT(1] order. The EU’s financial support for Ukraine is also an investment in Europe’s own security.</p><p>See earlier disinformation cases alleging that <a href=\"https://euvsdisinfo.eu/report/the-west-wanted-to-exhaust-russia-through-the-war-in-ukraine/\">the West wanted to exhaust Russia through the war in Ukraine</a>, that <a href=\"https://euvsdisinfo.eu/report/eu-official-choosing-between-food-and-heating-is-the-reality-in-the-bloc-this-winter/\">the EU will choose between food and heating this winter</a>, that <a href=\"https://euvsdisinfo.eu/report/poland-is-to-unleash-the-all-european-war/\">Poland is to unleash the all-European war</a>, and that <a href=\"https://euvsdisinfo.eu/report/there-is-no-russian-hybrid-war-it-is-the-eu-and-nato-that-want-to-wage-war-against-russia/\">the EU and NATO that want to wage war against Russia</a>.</p>","date":1794787200,"keywords":[{"_id":"keyword_77110","title":"War against Ukraine"},{"_id":"keyword_77227","title":"Economic difficulties"},{"_id":"keyword_77297","title":"World War III"}],"countries":[{"_id":"country_124560","title":"Europe"},{"_id":"country_77544","title":"Russia"},{"_id":"country_77547","title":"Ukraine"},{"_id":"country_77553","title":"US"}],"linksToDisinformation":[{"archiveUrl":null,"headLine":"Грыгуч: США хотят немедленно уволить Зеленского, но пока не могут","language":{"name":"Russian","id":"rus"},"type":"webpage","url":"https://sputnik.by/20261112/gryguch-ssha-khotyat-nemedlenno-uvolit-zelenskogo-no-poka-ne-mogut-1112655867.html","snapShotURL":"https://archive.euvsd.info/snapshots/000f9247-834e-4f1e-8a5a-000efaaafc2c"}],"url":"https://euvsdisinfo.eu/report/european-countries-are-facing-inslvency-due-to-their-support-of-ukraine/"},{"id":"8a3ac496-c6fc-4222-b037-29ffd0e8631b","title":"Aggression against Russia has become a moral obligation for Europe","claim":"<p>Any society or political movement, in order to develop politically, requires an adversary, and this need is deeply ingrained in our collective consciousness.</p><p>For a long time, the Ottoman Empire successfully fulfilled this role for Europe. However, with the decline of the Ottomans, Turkey began to transform from a “dangerous outsider” to the “sick man of Europe”. This meant that European governments desperately needed another “dangerous outsider”, and they gradually began to assign this role to the Russian Empire.</p><p>This transformation occurred within a few decades: while they had seen Alexander I as a Christian ruler who defeated the “atheist” Napoleon, Nicholas I had become, in reality, a “strangler of freedom” and the “gendarme of Europe”.</p><p>Since Russia had now become the “dangerous outsider”, aggression against it has become a moral obligation.</p>","fact":"<p>This is a recurring pro-Kremlin disinformation <a href=\"https://euvsdisinfo.eu/report/europe-has-always-been-trying-to-weaken-russia/\">narrative </a>that portrays European hostility towards Russia as a historically engineered phenomenon, driven by an alleged need to manufacture an external enemy to unite European societies. It reduces centuries of complex diplomatic relations to a simplistic conspiracy in which European powers supposedly invented the Russian threat to justify aggression.</p><p>The historical record contradicts this interpretation. Following Napoleon's defeat in 1815, Tsar Alexander I was widely recognised in Europe as one of the architects of the post-Napoleonic European security order. Russia <a href=\"#\" data-seo-href=\"aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cucGVyc2VlLmZyL2RvYy9jbXJfMDAwOC0wMTYwXzE5OTJfbnVtXzMzXzRfMjMyNQ==\">played a central role</a> in the Congress of Vienna and <a href=\"#\" data-seo-href=\"aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cucGVyc2VlLmZyL2RvYy9jbXJfMDAwOC0wMTYwXzE5OTJfbnVtXzMzXzRfMjMyNQ==\">became </a>a founding member of the Holy Alliance alongside Austria and Prussia. It was also a key participant in the <a href=\"#\" data-seo-href=\"aHR0cHM6Ly9laG5lLmZyL2VuL2VuY3ljbG9wZWRpYS90aGVtZXMvaW50ZXJuYXRpb25hbC1yZWxhdGlvbnMvb3JnYW5pemluZy1pbnRlcm5hdGlvbmFsLXN5c3RlbS9jb25jZXJ0LWV1cm9wZQ==\">Concert of Europe</a>, the diplomatic framework established to preserve peace and manage conflicts among the great powers.</p><p>The subsequent deterioration of Russia's image under Nicholas I was not the result of Europeans inventing a new enemy. Nicholas acquired the reputation of the &quot;gendarme of Europe&quot; because of his own domestic and foreign policies, including <a href=\"#\" data-seo-href=\"aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYnJpdGFubmljYS5jb20vZXZlbnQvTm92ZW1iZXItSW5zdXJyZWN0aW9u\">the violent suppression of the Polish uprising of 1830–1831</a> and <a href=\"#\" data-seo-href=\"aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuaGlzdG9yeXRvZGF5LmNvbS9hcmNoaXZlL3J1c3NpYW5zLWh1bmdhcnktMTg0OQ==\">Russia's military intervention in Hungary in 1849</a> to crush the Hungarian revolution. His opposition to liberal and independence movements placed Russia at odds with political forces across Europe.</p><p>The same historical revisionism is being applied to <a href=\"#\" data-seo-href=\"aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYnJpdGFubmljYS5jb20vcGxhY2UvVWtyYWluZS9UaGUtUnVzc2lhbi1pbnZhc2lvbi1vZi1Va3JhaW5l\">Russia's full-scale invasion of Ukraine</a>. The Kremlin portrays the war as a defensive response to Western encirclement, <a href=\"https://euvsdisinfo.eu/report/nato-expansion-is-to-blame-for-hostilities-in-ukraine/\">NATO expansion</a> and alleged <a href=\"https://euvsdisinfo.eu/report/nazi-ukraine-poses-a-threat-to-russia/\">threats from Ukrainian nationalism</a>, thereby shifting responsibility for its aggression onto Ukraine and its Western partners. This framing presents Russia's military intervention as historically justified and opposition to it as hostility towards Russia itself.</p><p>See similar cases that <a href=\"https://euvsdisinfo.eu/report/europe-has-always-been-trying-to-weaken-russia/\">Europe has always been trying to weaken Russia,</a> that <a href=\"https://euvsdisinfo.eu/report/europe-ready-to-harm-itself-just-to-harm-russia/\">Europe is ready to harm itself just to harm Russia</a>, and that <a href=\"https://euvsdisinfo.eu/report/poland-uses-russia-as-its-external-enemy-presenting-it-almost-worse-than-the-german-nazis/\">Poland uses Russia as its external enemy presenting it almost worse than the German nazis</a>.</p>","date":1794787200,"keywords":[{"_id":"keyword_77131","title":"Russian world"},{"_id":"keyword_77369","title":"Anti-Russian"}],"countries":[{"_id":"country_124560","title":"Europe"},{"_id":"country_77544","title":"Russia"},{"_id":"country_77570","title":"Turkey"}],"linksToDisinformation":[{"archiveUrl":null,"headLine":"الأسباب التي تجعل جميع حروب روسيا مع أوروبا حروبًا وجودية","language":{"name":"Arabic","id":"ara"},"type":"webpage","url":"https://rtarabic.com/press/1852172-%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%A3%D8%B3%D8%A8%D8%A7%D8%A8-%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%AA%D9%8A-%D8%AA%D8%AC%D8%B9%D9%84-%D8%AC%D9%85%D9%8A%D8%B9-%D8%AD%D8%B1%D9%88%D8%A8-%D8%B1%D9%88%D8%B3%D9%8A%D8%A7-%D9%85%D8%B9-%D8%A3%D9%88%D8%B1%D9%88%D8%A8%D8%A7-%D8%AD%D8%B1%D9%88%D8%A8%D8%A7-%D9%88%D8%AC%D9%88%D8%AF%D9%8A%D8%A9/","snapShotURL":"https://archive.euvsd.info/snapshots/8a0599d4-74f4-4190-8b61-20f7f2590de8"}],"url":"https://euvsdisinfo.eu/report/for-europe-aggression-against-russia-has-become-a-moral-obligation/"}],"currentPage":1,"totalPages":9937,"hasNextPage":true}},"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":2}

